<title>SPAIN: Protocol to cut Endesa income by 25 bln pta.</title>
<headline>Protocol to cut Endesa income by 25 bln pta.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's electricity protocol, a set of guidelines aimed at liberalising the power sector and making it more competitive, will reduce Endesa's annual income by less than 25 billion pesetas, Secretary of State for Energy, Nemesio Fernandez Cuesta told reporters in parliament on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The protocol was signed in December.</p>
<p>Fernandez said Endesa may also see efficiency savings or capital gains.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
